    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is the behavior of open brackets (`(`, `[`, `{`, `<`). [Here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/02e22656f1b78aa9f9a678e0ff31b62bbaf0dee6/doc/mini-surround.txt#L158-L169) are examples and [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/02e22656f1b78aa9f9a678e0ff31b62bbaf0dee6/doc/mini-surround.txt#L189-L190) is this in documentation.\r\n\r\nYou have two options:\r\n- Use corresponding close bracket (`)`, `]`, `}`, `>`) to add brackets without spaces. This is preferred solution.\r\n- Make custom surroundings:\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.surround').setup({\r\n  custom_surroundings = {\r\n    ['('] = { input = { '%b()', '^.().*().$' }, output = { left = '(', right = ')' } },\r\n    ['['] = { input = { '%b[]', '^.().*().$' }, output = { left = '[', right = ']' } },\r\n    ['{'] = { input = { '%b{}', '^.().*().$' }, output = { left = '{', right = '}' } },\r\n    ['<'] = { input = { '%b<>', '^.().*().$' }, output = { left = '<', right = '>' } },\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n``` ",
            "created_at": "2022-09-10T16:31:49Z",
